From bdf385d44748457148e7a8f4ad9355229ba5cc71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 11:17:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: per-engagement Reputation Manager findings page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the bigger RM gap flagged this session: the 6 chat-only adhoc
actions (live AI-engine spot-check, crisis threshold stress-test,
draft-response, and Twitter/Trustpilot/Reddit deep scans) had no natural
UI home because no page anywhere showed one client's actual findings —
those existed only per-run (/dashboard/runs/[id]) or aggregated across
the whole workspace (/dashboard/reputation-manager). This adds that page:
/dashboard/engagements/[id]/skills/reputation-manager, linked from each
RM worker card on WorkersPanel ("Findings", mirroring Showtime's
"Pipeline" link).

New /api/engagements/[id]/rep-findings route reads the client's most
recent rows across all 5 RM ingestion tables (engine findings, Trustpilot
reviews, Reddit/Twitter mentions, incidents) — the first route to scope
any of them to one engagement rather than one run or the whole workspace.
A new /rep-findings/trigger route dispatches all 6 adhoc actions through
the exact same chat-skill-trigger.ts functions Teammates chat already
uses, including a per-finding "Draft a response" button wired to the real
finding text.

Also fixes a real bug found while building this: the run-detail page's
SkillView switch had no case for any of the 6 adhoc skill names, so
clicking "View run" on one of them rendered PinDownView — Showtime
script/brief/page-audit deliverables that are always null for an RM run.
Added skillRuns.summary to the detail route's select (it was queried but
never selected) and a generic AdhocRunSummaryView for these 6 skills,
which is all their real output actually is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
